**Finding: missing — critical.**

The Agreement has no indemnification section at all. Section 20 is absent from the outline entirely, yet the document repeatedly assumes it exists:

- § 9.3 conditions a Customer termination right on Vendor's inability to "provide the remedies required by Section 20.5" (dangling cross-reference);
- § 19.4 preserves remedies for "indemnified claims";
- § 21.3 carves "indemnification obligations" out of the liability cap;
- § 30.5 refers to "an indemnified party" and "vested indemnity rights".

No Vendor IP or misconduct indemnity exists anywhere, which is walk-away territory under INDEMN.

**Cure (preferred level):** inserted new § 20.1 immediately after § 19.5 — Vendor defends and indemnifies Customer and its Affiliates against third-party claims for (a) IP infringement/misappropriation by the Services or Deliverables, (b) Vendor's breach of Applicable Law, (c) unauthorized access to or disclosure of Customer Data caused by Vendor, and (d) Vendor's gross negligence or wilful misconduct, with prompt notice, Vendor control of the defence, and reasonable cooperation; any Customer indemnity is expressly limited to Customer-provided content and Customer's breach of Applicable Law.

I targeted preferred rather than fallback deliberately: the fallback's 3× annual-fees super-cap would be a downgrade from § 21.3, which currently leaves indemnification obligations outside the liability cap. I therefore omitted the super-cap and the procure/modify/replace/refund remedies as fallback-only elements, keeping the insertion to the shortest text carrying every preferred element.
